meta {
  name: List Permissions
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/permissions
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{ownerAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("covers the whole vocabulary", function () {
    expect(res.getBody()).to.be.an("array").with.length.of.at.least(39);
  });

  test("carries display metadata, not just keys", function () {
    const first = res.getBody()[0];
    expect(first).to.have.property("key");
    expect(first).to.have.property("label");
    expect(first).to.have.property("kind");
    expect(first).to.have.property("group");
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /permissions — the permission catalog

  Every permission the system recognises, with the label, description and
  grouping a role editor needs. Sorted by `kind` then `sortOrder`.

  **Module:** none (`@SkipModule()`) — administering permissions cannot depend
  on which pages the agency has switched on.
  **Permission:** `agency:roles:read`
  **Data scope:** not applicable; the catalog is global.

  ## Why global rows

  The catalog carries no `agencyId`. The 39 permission strings are compiled into
  91 guard decorators, so a per-agency catalog would let configuration delete a
  permission the code still requires — which denies everyone, with no error
  anywhere. Per-tenant availability is a separate question, answered by
  `agency.modules[key].enabled` and applied when a user's set is resolved.

  ## Query params

  | Param | Type | Notes |
  |---|---|---|
  | includeDeprecated | `"true"` | Include retired keys. Off by default: they are kept only because `rolePermissions` rows may still reference them, and offering one in a picker would invite granting a permission nothing checks. |

  ## Response

  ```json
  [
    {
      "_id": "…",
      "key": "leads:read",
      "kind": "module",
      "moduleKey": "leads",
      "resource": "leads",
      "action": "read",
      "label": "View Leads",
      "description": "Priority contact list and lead records.",
      "group": "Pages",
      "sortOrder": 10,
      "assignableToUser": true,
      "isDeprecated": false
    }
  ]
  ```

  `kind` is `module` (a page, 26 of them), `agency` (an admin capability, 8) or
  `platform` (above the tenant boundary, 5). Only `module` permissions have
  `assignableToUser: true` — admin capabilities come from role membership alone.

  ## Errors
  - `401 Unauthorized` — no or invalid token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — missing `agency:roles:read`.
}
